              "parent_id": "7dfdcfb4-45d6-4a01-9ce0-2f6f7634f5f9",
              "text": "I’d avoid both a full one-week slip and cutting import outright. **Time-box the schema review, keep the conference launch, and ship import behind a pilot-only flag** if the review clears a defined safety threshold. That preserves the announcement while protecting the capability the two pilot customers explicitly requested. If the schema remains unsafe at the cutoff, delay only import—not the whole launch—and communicate a firm follow-up date. This balances the conference constraint with customer commitments. Sources: Priya Shah (`7bb0eb4a…`), Rahul Mehta (`9a825b1d…`), Sara Kim (`17a2ebec…`).",
